<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Peloponnesian League</h1><p class="st-meta">550 BCE – 366 BCE (approx.) · capital Sparta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Sparta's network of alliances, the leading military coalition of classical Greece and Athens' opponent in the Peloponnesian War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The league grew in the mid-6th century BCE when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a>, after defeating <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tegea">Tegea</a> around 550 BCE, turned from conquest to alliance. City by city, Peloponnesian states such as Tegea, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corinth">Corinth</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/elis">Elis</a> and later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/megara">Megara</a> swore to have the same friends and enemies as the Lacedaemonians and to follow them wherever they led.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>There was no common treasury or capital beyond <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a>. Each ally was bound to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> by its own treaty; from the late 6th century a congress of allies voted on war, each city having one vote, and Sparta commanded the joint army. Sparta favoured friendly oligarchies in member cities. The league formed the core of Greek resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 480-479 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>It fought and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a> (431-404 BCE), but the Theban victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a> in 371 BCE and invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a> broke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta's</a> hold. The liberation of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/messene">Messenia</a> and separate peace deals by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corinth">Corinth</a> and others in 366-365 BCE ended the league.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/peloponnesian-league.jpg" alt="Peloponnesian League" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: Marsyas; derivative work by Aeonx · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Peloponnesian_War_431_BC-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>550 BCE – 366 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sparta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cleomenes I, Archidamus II, Agesilaus II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek (Doric)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lacedaemonians and their allies</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-458&amp;focus=peloponnesian-league" aria-label="Peloponnesian League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5242 842 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Peloponnesian League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5562 1098L5572 1070M5562 1098L5582 1068M5562 1098L5566 1068M5562 1098L5537 1079M5562 1098L5559 1080M5562 1098L5561 1085M5562 1098L5565 1073M5562 1098L5578 1080M5562 1098L5584 1084M5562 1098L5562 1098M5562 1098L5562 1066M5562 1098L5557 1077"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5572 1070h0M5582 1068h0M5566 1068h0M5537 1079h0M5559 1080h0M5561 1085h0M5565 1073h0M5578 1080h0M5584 1084h0M5562 1098h0M5562 1066h0M5557 1077h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5562 1098h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5562 1098h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sparta. <a href="/atlas?year=-458&amp;focus=peloponnesian-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

